f an integrated qualitative process evaluation in providing evidence to discontinue the intervention in one arm of a trial of a decision support tool</article-title><source>Qual Saf Health Care</source><volume>16</volume><fpage>224</fpage><lpage>229</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17545351</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pmed-0040258-b011"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group><name><surname>Weaver</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Renton</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Tyrer</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Ritchie</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><year>1996</year><article-title>Combining qualitative studies with randomised controlled trials is often useful</article-title><source>BMJ</source><volume>313</volume><fpage>629</fpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8806277</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pmed-0040258-b012"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group><name><surname>Hammersley</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group><year>1992</year><article-title>Deconstructing the qualitative&#x02013;quantitative divide</article-title><person-group person-group-type="editor"><name><surname>Brannen</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><comment>editor</comment><source>Mixing methods: Qualitative and quantitative research</source><publisher-loc>Aldershot (United Kingdom)</publisher-loc><publisher-name>Avebury</publisher-name><fpage>39</fpage><lpage>55</lpage></citation></ref></ref-list><fn-group><fn id="fn1" fn-type="current-aff"><p>The <italic>PLoS Medicine</italic> Editors are Virginia Barbour, Barbara Cohen, Paul Chinnock, Larry Peiperl, and Gavin Yamey.</p></fn></fn-group></back></article>